SUMMARY:Blue Ridge Parkway Walkers Knob Overlook to Cane Gap. Out/Back FIT
 NESS HIKE.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Revised to a 10 mile single opti
 on Hike**\n\n**It is an honor to be selected to lead this hike...thank you
  Allen for your confidence in me. I hope we don't end up in Tennessee\, or
  Oklahoma\, or something.**\n\n**MEETUP OPTION:**\n**Carpool option 1:** M
 eet at **8:45 am**\, at the Folk Art Center to follow or carpool.\n**Carpo
 ol option 2:** Meet at Weaverville Ingles (across from Publix) near gas pu
 mps at **8:35am**. We will travel up Ox Creek to BPR so you could also mee
 t us there if easier(approx 8:55am).\n\nPease post if you plan to carpool 
 and where you will join the caravan\, otherwise see you at the TH at 9:30 
 am. Walkers Knob Overlook Trailhead is approximately 40 minutes from Folk 
 Art Center and 45-50 minutes from Ingles Weaverville.\n\n**HIKE DESCRIPTIO
 N\;**\nThis is an O&B\, 10 mile back country hike passing Point Misery\, L
 ittle Butt\, and Big Butt with a turn around after 5 miles. Lunch at eithe
 r Big Butt or Little Butt on the return.\nThere are over 350 well-crafted 
 wooden steps ( out and back) on a trail which is mostly under a deciduous 
 forest. The trail is maintained by the NC High Peaks Association. T**he el
 evation gain estimates is approximately 2000 feet\, level 6\\*.** High Mou
 ntain Temperatures on this hike are tipically 10+ degrees cooler than Ashe
 ville.\n\n**PACE:** Fitness hikes proceed at a steady pace averaging 2.5 M
 PH on climbs and/or rugged trail conditions\, and 3+ MPH on level/downgrad
 e sections with brief regrouping at trail intersections\, or as needed. **
 There are plenty of cardiochallenges and endurance sections on this hike w
 hich is for conditioned hikers.** Please know your hiking abilities before
  signing on. Any questions please post on this meetuo site or message me.\
 n\n**DOGS:** Trail friendly dogs are welcome\n\n**Trailhead Directions**. 
 Put Walkers Knob Overlook into Google or Apple Maps. Big Butt Trail is adj
 acent to parking area.\n\nIf you sign up for this hike or waitlist and cha
 nge your mind go back to the RSVP link and cancel your reservation to free
  the space for other hikers.\n\n**Weather: Cancellation** and / rescheduli
 ng will be made on or before 7 AM hike day if inclimate weather forecasts 
 indicates potential unsuitable conditions.\n\n**DOGS:** Trail-friendly dog
 s welcome\n\n**\\*HIKE LEVELS**...are based on the total elevation gain (o
 r estimates).\nLevel (1) Up to 600 feet of elevation gain.\nLevel (2) 600'
 - 900'\; Level (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4) 1200' - 1500'\; Level (5) 1\,5
 00' - 1\,800'\; Level **(6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'**\; Level (7)\\* 2\,100' - 2
 \,400'\; Level (8) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level (9) 2700' - 3000' Level (10) 30
 00' - 4000'\;\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe organizer of this trip is 
 a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is
  only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event y
 ou acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks o
 f injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and a
 ssociated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to
  the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/t
 erms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/312212367
 /
