DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T130000
SUMMARY:Bent Creek: 7 mi 1000 ft elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens Sunday 5/3\, 8:00
  pm]**\n\nConsider this a true **moderate-level** hike\, somewhat longer a
 nd faster than my usual Friday morning jaunts. It's not an easy one\, and 
 not for beginners. We'll be covering 7 miles with at least a 2.5 mph pace.
 \n\nThanks to Todd for putting together this route\, largely on Lower Side
 hill Trail and South Ridge Rd. It's a pretty area deep into Bent Creek. Th
 e plan is for a "lollipop" with a short stem at the start and finish\, and
  a big loop the rest of the way.\n\nThere's good footing throughout\, with
  a combination of forest trails and gravel roads. If you're on the fence a
 bout poles\, you probably won't need them here. Bring water and a snack if
  you're inclined. There'll be a little break somewhere around the middle.\
 n\n**CARPOOLING TIME & PLACE**\n\nThere's very limited trailhead parking\,
  so we'll carpool from the Asheville Outlets behind the Waffle House (dire
 ctions below). Look for me and my silver Hyundai. Come early to allow for 
 traffic. We'll depart by 9:00 AM\n\nHere's the Waffle House location on Go
 ogle Maps:\n[https://goo.gl/maps/kjkQTmGQA7QNgbWLA](https://goo.gl/maps/kj
 kQTmGQA7QNgbWLA)\n\n**From Exit 33 on I-26\,**\n\n* Head south a short dis
 tance on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191) to the traffic light with Ingles on the rig
 ht and Waffle House on the left.\n* Turn Left into the Asheville Outlets.\
 n* Drive just past the Waffle House and turn left onto the parking lot acc
 ess road\, NOT into the Waffle House lot.\n* Take the first right. We'll p
 ark and meet in this area of the lot.\n\n**ALSO IMPORTANT**\n***Dogs.*** W
 ell-behaved dogs are welcome\, but U.S. Forest Service regulations require
  leashes. Wear sensible hiking boots. Bring some water. If you're on the f
 ence about hiking poles\, you probably don't need them for this one.\n\n**
 *Guests.*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they must join the Asheville 
 Hiking Group and sign up for the hike independently. Alternatively\, conta
 ct me in advance to ask if it's okay to bring a +1 after you've made it on
 to the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, we may be able to ad
 d your guest.\n\n**COURTESY TO WAITLISTERS** (Please abide!)\nOnly sign up
  if you \\*truly\\* plan to come. And if you're on the borderline of dropp
 ing out for any reason\, buck up and join us! I promise you'll be glad you
  did.\n\nIf you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as 
 soon as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please pl
 ease PLEASE don't ever be a "no-show" for any MeetUp events. Let your orga
 nizer know in advance.\n\nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep checking th
 e evening before. Despite what I wrote above\, we usually have last-minute
  dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and post a cancellation 
 message by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**Q
 UESTIONS?**\nIf you have any questions\, message me through MeetUp until 8
 :00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text
  or call me up to the start of the hike: (803) 767-3094.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville 
 Hiking Group (AHG) event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation t
 o and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own saf
 ety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioni
 ng\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and pro
 perty. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure y
 our safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibilit
 y for any damages or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314608183
 /
