SUMMARY:Scenic AVL  - Waynesville Way - Weekend Wildcard
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nCarpooling: Please announce in the
  chat if you would like to carpool. I recommend 8:55 from 16 Regent Park B
 lvd\, Asheville (near Sam's Club)\, but I am coming from Hendersonville\, 
 so I won't be there.\n\nRating: Strenuous for Distance\nDistance: 9 miles\
 nElevation Gain: 1000 feet\, in small chunks\nFeatures: Farmer's Market\, 
 Rural farm views\, neighborhood charm\, nice downtown.\nWildlife: No bears
 \, but there are lots of birds and a few cows.\nPace: 3.2 mph when moving\
 , but we will stop here and there.\nSurface: Road\nDogs: On leash\nRoute (
 reverse direction): [Waynesville Way](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/re
 cording/activity-november-11-2024-5e38810)\n[.](https://maps.app.goo.gl/dr
 FxX2TaTrZKWX9F8)\nCoffee Break: We are walking the route in the opposite d
 irection from how we usually do it . We will stop for a break at the Farme
 r's Market at the Shelton House Museum.\n**[Special Instructions](https://
 maps.app.goo.gl/3LZwYE6S8TJRgXpQ6?g_st=ac)**[: If you are late\, meet us](
 https://maps.app.goo.gl/3LZwYE6S8TJRgXpQ6?g_st=ac) at the Shelton House fa
 rmers market\; we will arrive in 45 minutes from the start time (10:15).\n
 \nNo bathroom at the start. but there's woods.\n\n*Mountain Research Stati
 on: We are walking down Test Farm Road across the NC Agricultural Extensio
 n Mountain Research Station. Please sign in using the [Visitor Registratio
 n](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfDFCDqvA7x7AkL8A2jaLthTf2lSQB
 wlEyC99r-H4SVDsqQaA/viewform) website.\n\nScenic Asheville Series: This hi
 ke is a wildcard \, meaning that it can be a substitute for any of the oth
 er hikes.\nThere are [10 hikes ](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X
 Um-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?usp=drivesdk)in the series
 \; hike 9 of them and receive an [attractive badge ](https://docs.google.c
 om/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit)for your p
 ack. Badgers can always attend a hike\, even if on the waiting list. See o
 ur [highlights here](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8XthO
 FXxekBpt2LGP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/)!\n\nRSVP and On-Time Start:\n\n- Call (do
  not text) the hike leader on the day of the hike if you can't find the st
 art 828-290-0886\n*If you decide you cannot come\, please change your RSVP
 .\n\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking o
 n city streets that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for the
 ir safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer
  and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to or
 ganize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowle
 dge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\
 , illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated w
 ith this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup
  terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
